afk: prompt wording only — mention jj alongside git in the hardcoded
prompts (system-prompt, orchestrate-notice, plan-mode-active,
commit-message-system).

Motivation: this distribution mandates jj (profile/rules/jj-basics.md),
but omp's built-in prompts speak raw git (`git status`, branch talk,
commit instructions). Agents follow the nearest instruction, so the
built-ins must at least name the jj equivalents (`jj st`,
`jj describe`) instead of contradicting the rule files.

What must survive a rebase:
- No behavior change, prose only. If upstream rewrote these prompt
  files, re-apply the intent (jj named wherever git subcommands are
  prescribed) rather than the exact wording. (18.0.11 compressed all
  four prompts; the same four spots were re-worded in place.)

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream rewrote system-prompt.md (the
destructive-commands line now reads "destructive git commands or delete
unrelated code", sections renumbered) and orchestrate-notice.md (dispatch
step now mentions auto-delivered results / `wait`). The same four spots
were re-worded in place against the new text; no other built-in prompt
newly prescribes state-changing git subcommands (jevify-notice's read-only
`git show` works unchanged in a colocated repo).

Rebased 18.18.0 -> 18.20.3: upstream reworded system-prompt.md again
("code your change makes obsolete is in scope"; the critical block now
says "run git to validate them"); both spots name git/jj again. The new
ovnfs "Separate checkouts" section only forbids git worktree add/clone,
so it is left alone.

